This is not true at this point in the series. `introspection.c` dereferences
`ctlvdev->dynamic_ops_count`, `->transition_lock`, `->state_generation` and
->disabled, and none of these exist in the `struct ctlv_device` that patch 10
creates (they are added by the dispatch patch). It also calls `ctlv_op_find()`,
which is only defined in `core.c`. So the file neither compiles nor links until
the last patch; "compile-checked" only holds if you do not actually compile it.
Either move the device fields into the patch that first uses them (here) or drop
the claim. Also note no `Documentation/ctlv` text or selftest accompanies the new
op-schema-get/ops-dump/families-dump behaviour, and the fragment/resume
semantics (entries split across fragments at member granularity, replayed
ancestor nests) are only discoverable from this code.

