> +/* A cursor packs the record and member where fragmentation resumes. */

The cursor is a client-supplied value (echoed back on continuation). Nothing
validates it: a member > END or record >= count just yields an empty or "done"
reply, which is harmless here, but the packing (48-bit record / 16-bit member)
is an implicit ABI of the opaque cursor and is used by only two of the three
dumps (op-schema-get uses a raw leaf ordinal). Three cursor encodings in one
file; consider documenting them as opaque.

