Orphan comment: it is not attached to any declaration (blank line follows
and then an unrelated struct). It also hides a cost: a continuation re-walks the
whole schema from the start, skipping 'resume' leaves, so dumping a schema of L
leaves in k fragments is O(k*L) and each fragment replays the ancestor nests
(see `ctlv_introspection_open()`). Bounded by schema size, but worth noting.

