The count is exactly the worst case (3 + 4 blob + 2 unit/scale + 1 reenters = 10),
so the `WARN_ON_ONCE` in `ctlv_introspection_field()` is a dead branch unless a field
is added. The fields[] array costs 10 * 24 bytes = 240 bytes on the stack, and
is instantiated in every level of the `ctlv_introspection_node()` <->
`ctlv_introspection_children()` recursion (up to `CTLV_MAX_NEST_DEPTH` = 32 levels,
plus the cursors), i.e. >8 KiB of kernel stack in one ioctl, on top of the
ioctl path. Allocate it once in the walk (the frames are already heap
allocated for this very reason) or emit directly without staging.

