Both `query_more` and `query_done` are passed generation 0 here. Fine, but note the
same fragmenting cursor is therefore valid across device state changes; an
op's description is static, OK. The cursor is the leaf ordinal and it must be
non-zero and different from `ctx->frag`.cursor: if the first leaf does not fit
(buffer smaller than `ctlv_op_schema_get`'s declared `query_reply_min_len`) the
core WARNs and returns `-EINVAL` rather than an informative error; ensure the
generator's min length covers one nest-start plus one leaf at the deepest
nesting (32 levels of nest headers).

