Summary of the most serious issues:

 - The commit message claim that `introspection.c` can be compile-checked is
   false: it uses `ctlv_device` fields (`transition_lock`, `state_generation`,
   `dynamic_ops_count`, disabled) and `ctlv_op_find()` that only appear in the final
   dispatch patch. Series is not bisectable for this file.
 - Large per-level stack use (10-entry field array in every level of a
   32-deep recursion), and unbounded fill-to-fill recursion not covered by the
   depth guard.
 - Needless `GFP_KERNEL` bitmap allocation per fragment plus awkward double
   ownership; default: cases that silently map unknown enum members to
   `event_record_max_len` / query members.
 - Inconsistent cursor encodings, `-EOPNOTSUPP` for an unknown op id, orphan
   comment, broken `guard()` formatting, and no documentation of the fragment
   resume semantics.

Thanks,
Reviewer
